# newshell.policy - who may call which protected method, and where.
# Architecture: Tom Dyer. Written by Claude (Opus 5.5).
#
# verdict principal class      method  path        ('*' matches anything)
# First matching line wins. No match = deny. A path matches itself and
# everything below it. A path through a symbolic link is always denied.
# Workspace~run is judged as run:PROGRAM (run:make, run:./hello/hello);
# a method ending in * is a prefix (run:./* is any program inside the
# workspace). JobBoard~submit has no path, so its rules use *.
# Principals: llm (code an LLM proposed, run with ~run), console (a person
# typing at nsh).
allow   llm       FileSystem   create   /tmp
allow   llm       FsFile       edit     /tmp
allow   llm       FileEditor   addline  /tmp
allow   llm       JobBoard     submit   *
allow   llm       Workspace    run:unzip  /tmp
allow   llm       Workspace    run:make   /tmp
allow   llm       Workspace    run:./*    /tmp
allow   llm       Workspace    remove   /tmp
allow   console   JobBoard     submit   *
allow   console   *            *        /tmp
deny    *         *            *        *
